  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197934",
      "title": "Supporting Different Editing Modes & Using Route Parameters",
      "lectureOrder": 138,
      "videoOrder": 134,
      "sourceHash": "2eaf421813a3115d7514d4a8edd1c9bf4e58831bf8bc32d387e8d37e5cfd16e3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.448,
          "end": 3.281,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmuller] So let's now work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.281,
          "end": 7.47,
          "en": "on those modes that we can enter inside of ManageExpense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.38,
          "end": 11.51,
          "en": "Now when I say modes, I simply mean the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.51,
          "end": 15,
          "en": "that we can either be adding a new expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15,
          "end": 18.85,
          "en": "if we click this plus here or editing an existing expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.85,
          "end": 22.2,
          "en": "if we click on an existing expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 24.99,
          "en": "We open the same screen in both cases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.99,
          "end": 29.99,
          "en": "but I actually want to do different things on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.34,
          "end": 32.46,
          "en": "Later in the next course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.46,
          "end": 35.2,
          "en": "when we add some real user input elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.2,
          "end": 39.22,
          "en": "I want to either have some pre-filled input elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.22,
          "end": 40.75,
          "en": "versus empty elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.75,
          "end": 43.013,
          "en": "For the moment, I wanna change the title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.21,
          "end": 45.96,
          "en": "So therefore, here in ManageExpense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.96,
          "end": 50.23,
          "en": "we need a way of finding out why this screen was opened.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.23,
          "end": 52.81,
          "en": "Is it to edit or to add?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.81,
          "end": 56.68,
          "en": "And we can utilize one important piece of information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.68,
          "end": 58.88,
          "en": "which we need to pass to this screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.88,
          "end": 61.87,
          "en": "if we are editing anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.87,
          "end": 64.54,
          "en": "And that's the idea of the expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.54,
          "end": 68.24,
          "en": "If we tap an expense, so here an ExpenseItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.24,
          "end": 70.14,
          "en": "and we then navigate to ManageExpense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.42,
          "end": 73.92,
          "en": "we will need to forward some information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.92,
          "end": 75.86,
          "en": "to this screen anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.86,
          "end": 78.41,
          "en": "We will need to forward the idea of the expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.41,
          "end": 79.59,
          "en": "that we wanna edit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.59,
          "end": 82.38,
          "en": "because we need that inside of the screen then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 87.38,
          "en": "to load the data, to know which expense to delete and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.27,
          "end": 90.4,
          "en": "Therefore here, in ExpenseItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.4,
          "end": 92.53999999999999,
          "en": "I'll add a second parameter value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.53999999999999,
          "end": 94.94,
          "en": "a second argument to the navigate method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.87,
          "end": 99.12,
          "en": "and pass my expenseId in this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.12,
          "end": 101.71000000000001,
          "en": "which is my second parameter value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.71000000000001,
          "end": 104.72999999999999,
          "en": "And for this, I expect to get the ID of the expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.72999999999999,
          "end": 108.02000000000001,
          "en": "for which this item was rendered as a prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.02000000000001,
          "end": 110.52000000000001,
          "en": "So with that, we set some route parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.52000000000001,
          "end": 114.08,
          "en": "that are provided to this Tubi loaded screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.08,
          "end": 118.81,
          "en": "And we only do this here, not in app JS for this plus icon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.81,
          "end": 121.25,
          "en": "because there, we're creating a new expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.25,
          "end": 124.89,
          "en": "therefore we have no idea of some existing expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.89,
          "end": 127.153,
          "en": "that should be forwarded to that screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.45,
          "end": 130.4,
          "en": "Therefore, in ManageExpense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.4,
          "end": 133.36,
          "en": "we can now extract that parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.36,
          "end": 136.97,
          "en": "and we know that if we have an ID, an expense ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.97,
          "end": 140.64,
          "en": "that we are editing and that if we have no expense ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.64,
          "end": 141.603,
          "en": "we're adding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.57999999999998,
          "end": 144.44,
          "en": "Therefore, here we can use this route prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.44,
          "end": 146.02,
          "en": "which we get automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.02,
          "end": 149.57999999999998,
          "en": "since this is a component that's loaded as a screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.57999999999998,
          "end": 152.42000000000002,
          "en": "This route prop is provided by react navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.42000000000002,
          "end": 153.93,
          "en": "as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.93,
          "end": 157.64,
          "en": "And we can use this route prop to extract the ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.64,
          "end": 159.57,
          "en": "the parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.57,
          "end": 162.373,
          "en": "So for that, we can get our editedExpenseId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.62,
          "end": 166.947,
          "en": "by accessing route.params.expenseId.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.2,
          "end": 170.17000000000002,
          "en": "And it's expenseId written like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.17000000000002,
          "end": 173.17000000000002,
          "en": "because that's the naming I chose in ExpenseItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.17000000000002,
          "end": 175.85,
          "en": "for configuring this parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.85,
          "end": 178.11,
          "en": "If you chose a different value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.11,
          "end": 180.223,
          "en": "you have to use a different value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.43,
          "end": 184.23,
          "en": "Now it is possible that we load this screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.23,
          "end": 185.96,
          "en": "without any params.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.96,
          "end": 188.37,
          "en": "In that case, params would be undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.37,
          "end": 191.1,
          "en": "and trying to access a property like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.1,
          "end": 192.323,
          "en": "would cause an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 193.26,
          "end": 195.99,
          "en": "We can use this conditional operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 195.99,
          "end": 198.6,
          "en": "that's built into modern JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 198.6,
          "end": 201.48,
          "en": "to check if params is undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 201.48,
          "end": 204.55,
          "en": "in which case we don't drill into it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 204.55,
          "end": 207.18,
          "en": "So this code then is not executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.18,
          "end": 210.91,
          "en": "and this overall instead returns undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.91,
          "end": 214.23,
          "en": "If params happens to be defined, if it is an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.23,
          "end": 218.93,
          "en": "we do drill into it and we do get that expenseId value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.93,
          "end": 221.57,
          "en": "So that is a safe way of drilling into an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.57,
          "end": 223.053,
          "en": "which might be undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.9,
          "end": 228.85,
          "en": "Therefore we know, that if editedExpenseId is not undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.85,
          "end": 231.45,
          "en": "we are editing because we have an ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 231.45,
          "end": 235.25,
          "en": "And if it is undefined, we failed to retrieve an ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.25,
          "end": 236.823,
          "en": "which means we are adding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 237.78,
          "end": 239.46,
          "en": "Therefore, we can translate this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.46,
          "end": 243.497,
          "en": "into another helper constant, which I'll name isEditing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 244.63,
          "end": 249.14,
          "en": "And here I simply convert editedExpenseId into a Boolean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.14,
          "end": 252.13,
          "en": "by adding two exclamation marks in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.13,
          "end": 254.27,
          "en": "That's a common JavaScript trick,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 254.27,
          "end": 256.63,
          "en": "to convert a value into a Boolean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 256.63,
          "end": 261.07,
          "en": "because with that, we convert a falsy value into false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 261.07,
          "end": 263.283,
          "en": "and a truthy value into true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 264.16,
          "end": 266.84,
          "en": "So therefore, now we have true if we are editing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 266.84,
          "end": 268.373,
          "en": "and false otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 269.63,
          "end": 272.89,
          "en": "Now that information can be used to, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 272.89,
          "end": 274.26,
          "en": "set the title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 275.19,
          "end": 277.63,
          "en": "because I wanna set the title and the header,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 277.63,
          "end": 279.913,
          "en": "based on whether we're adding or editing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 280.86,
          "end": 284.08,
          "en": "Now we also learned how we can update the options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 284.08,
          "end": 287.27,
          "en": "of a screen from inside that screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 287.27,
          "end": 292.27,
          "en": "We can do that with help of the navigation prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 292.3,
          "end": 295.93,
          "en": "which we also get here, since this is a screen component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 295.93,
          "end": 299.72,
          "en": "And on this prop, we can call the setOptions method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 299.72,
          "end": 302.24,
          "en": "which takes an options object which allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 302.24,
          "end": 304.95,
          "en": "to set values like a title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 304.95,
          "end": 307.69,
          "en": "So here we can then, for example, set the title too",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 307.69,
          "end": 309.04,
          "en": "and then check if isEditing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 311.72,
          "end": 313.17,
          "en": "and if this is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 313.17,
          "end": 317.93,
          "en": "using a ternary expression, we say Edit Expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 317.93,
          "end": 322.563,
          "en": "if this is false so in the else case, we say Add Expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 323.5,
          "end": 325.45,
          "en": "So this is using a ternary expression",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 325.45,
          "end": 327.163,
          "en": "to set the title dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 328.01,
          "end": 330.55,
          "en": "As you learned in the earlier sections though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 330.55,
          "end": 332.9,
          "en": "you shouldn't call setOptions like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 332.9,
          "end": 334.8,
          "en": "directly in the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 334.8,
          "end": 337.23,
          "en": "instead you should wrap it with useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 337.23,
          "end": 341.58,
          "en": "or to avoid that it's flickering initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 341.58,
          "end": 346.58,
          "en": "with useLayoutEffect, which is a hook imported from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 348.74,
          "end": 352.37,
          "en": "useLayoutEffect takes a function that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 352.37,
          "end": 354.08,
          "en": "and an array of dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 354.08,
          "end": 357.94,
          "en": "that controls when this function should be re-executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 357.94,
          "end": 361.127,
          "en": "and we pass our setOptions code into this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 361.127,
          "end": 363.72,
          "en": "and then regarding those dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 363.72,
          "end": 366.42,
          "en": "our dependencies are the navigation prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 366.42,
          "end": 370.53,
          "en": "and the isEditing helper variable or a constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 370.53,
          "end": 373.7,
          "en": "If those change, we would have to re-render the title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 373.7,
          "end": 376.63,
          "en": "but in this app, this won't change dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 376.63,
          "end": 378.94,
          "en": "Still, we should add those dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 378.94,
          "end": 380.653,
          "en": "since this is a good practice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 381.57,
          "end": 385.7,
          "en": "So now with that, we can reflect the different modes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 385.7,
          "end": 389.12,
          "en": "If I save everything now, we should be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 389.12,
          "end": 391.95,
          "en": "to actually open this to add a new expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 391.95,
          "end": 394.523,
          "en": "and see Add Expense in the title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 395.72,
          "end": 399.11,
          "en": "And alternatively, if I click an existing item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 399.11,
          "end": 402,
          "en": "we see Added Expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 402,
          "end": 404.35,
          "en": "So this is working the way it should.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 404.35,
          "end": 406.933,
          "en": "And that's another major step forward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 407.89,
          "end": 411.7,
          "en": "As a next step, I want to add some content to this screen",
          "zh": ""
